       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Metformin 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day.** That is 3 times the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day, and the risk is lactic acidosis. A single 2,550 mg dose is also well above any standard single dose. The usual maximum is about 1,000 mg per dose for immediate-release.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This totals 2,550 mg/day, the maximum daily dose.\n- **2,550 mg/day total**, split differently. For example, 1,000 mg in the morning and 1,000 mg at lunch, with 550 mg in the evening, or another split you prefer.\n- A different dose entirely.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 2550 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was intentional."
