       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 7,650 mg/day of metformin is 3 times the maximum labeled daily dose. I know of no indication that supports it. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and gives no added glycemic benefit, because the dose-response curve plateaus well below this. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- Another dose within the labeled range\n\nIf you have an unusual clinical reason for this dose, such as a protocol or a trial, please take it through pharmacy review and your institution's high-alert or override process. I'm not the right safeguard for that.\n\nWhich of the options above would you like me to enter?"
